// marble-catcher-round — the round bowl, which is the shape the Quadrilla original has,
// carrying the same work the wedge got: the block plugs into a Ø30 socket on a low pad,
// the marble comes in through a port pierced through the wall, the wall is 2.5 mm and
// leans inwards at the top, and the floor falls to a shallow central depression with the
// original's ring of ten radial slots around it.
//
// Simulated: 98 % of marbles kept, 75 cm3. The wedge (the default `catcher`) keeps 100 %
// on 67 cm3 but looks nothing like the original — this is the one that does.
use <../lib.scad>

module mr_catcher_round() { marble_catcher_round(); }

mr_catcher_round();
